# Oob — code ownership and review routing
#
# Human approval rule (AGENTS.md §6): every declared feature merges only
# when Marshal merges it, after the required reviews (AGENTS.md §6
# rule 2) — his merge is the approval (GitHub can't record an author
# approving their own PR). This file routes every pull request to the
# owner for notification; CODEOWNERS review is deliberately not a
# branch-protection requirement.

*   @OnTheStruggleBus

# Role ownership — who BUILDS each area (process-level; roles are repo
# agents, not GitHub users). Reviews are oob-qa (bugs) and oob-architect
# (drift) on every PR, per AGENTS.md §6 rule 2:
#
#   /crates/                    → oob-dev-core builds; oob-architect designs first (ADR / issue note)
#   /flowgraphs/                → oob-dev-rf builds
#   Console SPA (location set by ADR when C0 starts) → oob-dev-console builds
#   /lab/, /ops/ci/             → oob-qa builds (capture rig, canary, evidence)
#   /ops/*.yaml                 → oob-dev-core builds; oob-architect owns the schema
#   /docs/ (ADRs, protocol/)    → oob-architect builds
#   /docs/ (research notes)     → oob-expert builds
#   /.github/agents/, /.claude/ → oob-scrum / oob-pm build (process coherence)
